# The AuthZEN wire types are GENERATED with LF line endings, and their currency
# is checked by a BYTE comparison against what the generator emits
# (tests/authzen_generated_types_are_current.rs). On a platform where git
# rewrites line endings at checkout, that comparison fails for a reason nobody
# changed - identical text, CRLF on disk, LF from the emitter.
#
# This repository has no Windows CI job today, so this is prophylactic. It is
# here anyway because the sibling Java SDK's Windows runner hit exactly that
# failure, and a latent trap that only bites the next person to add a runner is
# still a trap.
#
# Scoped rather than a repo-wide `* text=auto eol=lf`, because changing the
# checkout behaviour of every other file in the repository is a bigger decision
# than this lane.
src/authzen/types_gen.rs      text eol=lf
testdata/authzen-surface.json text eol=lf
